## What the viewer does for you

- **One worker.** Every document shares a single pdf.js worker (set `configurePdf({ sharedWorker: false })` to opt out).
- **Exact, cheap layout.** All page shells exist from the start with their real size, so scroll height and jumps are exact; only pages within `overscan` viewport heights get a bitmap.
- **Priority scheduler.** Visible pages render first, nearby pages next, thumbnails last. Work for pages that scroll away is cancelled, and re-queuing a page replaces its pending job.
- **Zoom without re-layout storms.** A zoom frame changes one CSS variable (`--pdf-scale`); the stretched bitmap stays until the sharp render lands. Text layers follow through CSS and are re-measured once zoom settles.
- **Sharp zoom-ins.** Zoomed-out pages render at up to 2× (`oversampling`), and a page stretched past 1.35× during a long zoom is refreshed once.
- **Bitmap cache.** Pages that scroll away keep their bitmap in a shared LRU cache (`configurePdf({ bitmapCacheBytes })`, default 192 MB, `0` disables), so scrolling back or changing columns redraws instantly.
- **Level of detail.** Pages narrower than `detailMinWidth` (260 CSS px) — thumbnail-sized spreads when zoomed out — skip their text layer and text indexing, so four-per-row layouts stay smooth.
- **Cached analysis.** `PaperState` accepts a `cache` (`KeyValueStore`, e.g. `indexedDbStore('papers')`): analysis results are stored by document fingerprint and reopened papers skip analysis.
- **Capped bitmaps.** `maxCanvasPixels` (16M device pixels) bounds memory per page at high zoom.
- **Shared text.** Page text is extracted and indexed once, then shared by the text layer, find, selection, annotations and paper analysis.
- **Thumbnails** are rendered lazily, at low priority, and cached per document.

<Demo example="stress" height={480} />

## Tuning

| Knob | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `overscan` | Fewer pages pre-rendered around the view (lower memory) or more (smoother fast scrolling) |
| `maxCanvasPixels` | Lower on memory-constrained devices |
| `oversampling={false}` | Saves memory when users rarely zoom |
| `detailMinWidth` | Width below which pages skip text layers (raise it for faster zoomed-out layouts) |
| `configurePdf({ bitmapCacheBytes })` | Memory for bitmaps of off-screen pages |
| `smoothZoom={false}` | Jump instead of easing |
| `columns="auto"` + `maxColumns` | Limit how many pages share a row when zooming out |

<Callout title="Research-paper analysis">
	<code>Paper.Root</code> analyses typical papers in 0.2–0.5 s; plot-heavy papers whose operator lists are expensive can take several seconds. Pass <code>auto=&#123;false&#125;</code> and call <code>paper.analyze()</code> when the user opens a paper panel if you want to defer it.
</Callout>
